{
  "topic": "midgley",
  "ttsScript": "One man caused more environmental damage than any organism in Earth's history. In 1921, Thomas Midgley invented a new fuel additive. Tetraethyl lead. He told reporters it was safe. He washed his hands in it. He knew it was poison. Then he did it again. In 1930, he invented Freon. The first CFC. It punched a hole in the ozone layer. One man. Two inventions. Lead poisoning killed millions. CFCs nearly destroyed the atmosphere. He won every award. The American Chemical Society gave him their highest honor. Twice. He never saw the damage. He died in 1944 — strangled by his own pulley system. The man who poisoned the planet couldn't save himself.",
